    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="1315" n="1274" sameAs="frus:frus1949v03/pg1274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Austria)/3–3049:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Legation in Austria
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-22T17:00:00-05:00">April 22, 1949—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>376. Re Legtel 336 March 30, rptd Paris 16 for
                        Harriman<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d647-f1"/>
                    Repto 254 rptd Washington Repto 3643<anchor n="2" xml:id="d647-f2"/> and
                    occupation costs. Dept plans immediate approach UK and French urging that (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) further imposition occupation costs on Austria
                    hampers reconstruction increases financial difficulties and counter to basic
                    objectives; (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) stating that US does not wish to
                    agree quadripartite demands until matter explored <pb facs="1316" n="1275"
                        xml:id="pg1275"/> governmental level; (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)
                    asking that they consider favorably pay as you go arrangement aimed to relieve
                    Austria of burden and isolate Soviet in any further demands.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d647-f3"/> Meanwhile careful study 336 Vienna March 30 leads to view
                    that it affords no real relief in terms of goods and services or financial
                    strain, and that substitution of franc and sterling purchasing power for
                    existing drawing rights gives mere appearance of pay as you go for UK and
                    France. Although this plan might have propaganda advantage, Aust imports would
                    remain unchanged and occupying forces demands for goods and services not be
                    diminished. Thus result might in fact be adverse public reaction and Soviet
                    attack.</p>
                <p>Since real objective to reduce diversion products from Aust uses and to lessen
                    inflationary pressure through spending by Military hope to persuade UK and Fr on
                    new policy. ECA concurs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d647-f1" n="1" xml:id="d647-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d647-f2" n="2" xml:id="d647-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; in it Harriman stated that he
                    considered the proposal for Austrian occupation costs to be included as part of
                    an intra-European payments scheme to be improper, and would in no way alleviate
                    the fiscal burden of occupation costs in Austria. (863.50/4–1249)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d647-f3" n="3" xml:id="d647-f3-content">
                <p>For the details of this approach see the note to the British and French
                    Embassies, <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
